en by\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nComparing $A$ with the rotation matrix, we have \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta >0$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta <0$ we must have that $\\theta $ lies in $4$th quadrant. \n\nDividing the first equation by the second gives\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nThe principal value $\\theta $ is\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ represents a rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ radians *clockwise* about the origin." 13194139534456 17592186045417 false] [17592186284730 1071 "Let $I=[0,2]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times \\{-i\\}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" 13194139534456 17592186045417 true] [17592186284730 1071 "Let $I=[0,2]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times {-i}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" 13194139534456 17592186045417 false] [17592186284730 1074 "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}=[0,1]\\times \\{-1\\}=\\{(k,-1)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(0,-1)$ to the point $(1,-1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/a3/a39443fd1b3764ff60c0c052085134ad7eeda6759c07c4d936fc03cd121f72dd.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times \\{-i\\}=\\{(k,-i)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(0,-i)$ to the point $(i,-i).$ \n\n![](images/7f/7f18af14c55acc4bc