ns $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n2x-8y+6z=-4\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=4y-3z-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4y-3z-2 \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$, $z$ (free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4y-3z-2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534456 17592186045417 true] [17592186400604 1074 "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-8y+6z=-4 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n2x-8y+6z=-4\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=4y-3z-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4y-3z-2 \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$, $z$ (free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4y-3z-2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\e